{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"During normal turning, significantly higher PMC-STN alpha coherence was observed in the TurnPre phase (p = 0.0045, Fig. 3A). In contrast, during turning freeze, there was an increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.048) and a decrease in M1-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.043) during the TurnStart phase.\",\n    \"The increased coherence between the PMC and STN may reflect a compensatory mechanism to maintain motor control in the face of disrupted cortical signals; however, this abnormal coupling could also contribute to the rigidity and motor impairments characteristic of FOG31,32.\",\n    \"Our analysis revealed that the decreases in the PMC alpha power (β = 0.154, p = 0.035) (Fig. 4A) and increases in PMC-STN alpha coherence (β = 0.205, p = 0.006) (Fig. 4B) during the TurnPre phase, but not the TurnStart phase, significantly predicted the freezing duration within the trial.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"Our analysis revealed that the decreases in the PMC alpha power (β = 0.154, p = 0.035) (Fig. 4A) and increases in PMC-STN alpha coherence (β = 0.205, p = 0.006) (Fig. 4B) during the TurnPre phase, but not the TurnStart phase, significantly predicted the freezing duration within the trial.\",\n    \"B Increased PMC-STN alpha coherence during the TurnPre phase (but not during the TurnStart phase) relative to walking predicted shorter freezing episodes (β = 0.205, p = 0.006).\",\n    \"B Freezing of Turning: A delayed and exaggerated increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence and concurrent decoupling of M1-STN alpha coherence was observed during the TurnStart phase.\",\n    \"We observed an increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence during TurnPre in normal turning, suggesting the role of PMC-STN connectivity in the initiation of the turning task. The increased coherence between the PMC and STN may reflect a compensatory mechanism to maintain motor control in the face of disrupted cortical signals; however, this abnormal coupling could also contribute to the rigidity and motor impairments characteristic of FOG31,32.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的基本电生理结果有全文依据：正常转弯的TurnPre阶段和冻结转弯的TurnStart阶段，PMC-STN alpha coherence均相对于Walk显著升高；原文讨论也确实提出了代偿性机制和可能参与FOG病理过程两种解释。但报告的概括存在重要不完整之处。原文第3.5节之后的第4节（Electrophysiological predictors of freezing severity）明确报告，TurnPre阶段PMC-STN alpha coherence与冻结持续时间显著相关（β=0.205，P=0.006），而TurnStart阶段没有显著预测作用。Figure 4的图注进一步明确指出，TurnPre阶段相对于walking增加的PMC-STN alpha coherence预测较短的冻结发作。这一结果为TurnPre阶段的保护性或代偿性解释提供了重要支持，也使TurnPre与TurnStart不能被视为具有相同意义的两种耦合增强现象。因此，如果报告仅依据两阶段的相干性升高对H4和H5作近似对称的解释，而没有充分纳入该回归结果，则属于部分支持但存在关键限定条件缺失，判定为partly，而不是no。指控者的核心描述有直接原文依据：TurnPre的回归结果、较短冻结持续时间的方向性关系，以及TurnStart的延迟性和增强性PMC-STN耦合与M1-STN解耦均有明确记载。需要保留的限定是，原文使用的是'may reflect a compensatory mechanism'，说明代偿作用属于可能的机制解释，而非已证实的因果关系。相关性不能证明PMC-STN耦合增强导致冻结减少，也不能证明其具有因果性的保护作用。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "c3214200-2a64-45b1-9e52-5d90f3049008", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261113T152005655290Z", "elapsed_seconds": 144.547, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T15:22:30.205171+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "c846be3ce62e9fc2bfaf8da9a77193d08d51bc94ca7f8526a1af4bb73acc121e", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261113T152005655290Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "c901f034c3680f7d08339d930625a5104f77676f668ea76f16c1c0e9da3bed5b"}}}
